                <pb facs="0336" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13603: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Spiker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-12T11:00:00+08:00">July 12, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of July 9, 4 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d227-f1"/>
                    Marshals Chen, Pai and other leading military and civil members of Southwest
                    Political Council yesterday addressed telegram to second plenary session at
                    Nanking urging adoption of the five point program proposed by Southwest June 22.
                    (See my telegram of June 23, noon, and June 29, 4 p.m.) Situation here remains
                    quiet.</p>
                <p>2. Sent to the Department, Peiping, Nanking, Shanghai and Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spiker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
